  "notes": "The page at rest: the title, the line that dates the board, the currency converter, its amount field and result box, and the metals card with its heading. `origin` is the title, because the page's frame and the app's frame are different heights and the design is the gaps between these boxes, not where the first one lands. `capture` is the converter card, because it is the region both clients draw identically; the metals card repeats the same shapes and is measured by its own boxes. Widths are left out of the title deliberately: its width is the run of text, not a decision. Colours are left out deliberately too - they are what the raster proves.",
